<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74848" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεκτ-ός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρέγω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stretched out,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. μελίαι</span> pikes <i>to be used for
				thrusting,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.543
			</span></i> ; so <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεκτὸν δόρυ</span>
			<i>pike,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παλτόν</span>
			(javelin), <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				10.1.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>longed for, desired,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὀ.</span>”
				<i>the object of appetency,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>de An.</u>
					433a18
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EN</u>
				1113a10
			</span></i>, al. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὀ. κινεῖ οὐ κινούμενον τῷ
					νοηθῆναι ἢ φαντασθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>de An.</u>
					433b11
				</span></i>
			 ; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεκτέος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.22
			</span></i>.</div>
